    "q-129430": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129430",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt{{m}^{2}{n}^{2}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${m}^{2}$ and ${n}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{m}^{2}{n}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{m\\cdot m\\cdot n\\cdot n} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{m\\cdot n\\cdot m\\cdot n} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(mn)\\cdot (mn)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(mn)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(mn)^{2}} & =|mn|\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
