    "q-129465": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129465",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{100}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${r}^{2}$ and $100$ are both perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{100}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{r}^{2}}{{10}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{r\\cdot r}{10\\cdot 10}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{r}{10}\\cdot \\frac{r}{10}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{r}{10})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{r}{10})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{r}{10}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|r|}{|10|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|r|}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
