    "q-129392": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129392",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{81{q}^{2}}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${p}^{2},81,$ and ${q}^{2}$ are all perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{81{q}^{2}}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{p}^{2}}{{9}^{2}\\cdot {q}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p\\cdot p}{9\\cdot 9\\cdot q\\cdot q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p\\cdot p}{9\\cdot q\\cdot 9\\cdot q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{p}{9q}\\cdot \\frac{p}{9q}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{p}{9q})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{p}{9q})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{p}{9q}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{|9q|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{|9|\\cdot |q|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|p|}{9|q|}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
