    "q-129471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129471",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25{y}^{2}}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${z}^{2},25,$ and ${y}^{2}$ are all perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25{y}^{2}}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z\\cdot z}{5\\cdot 5\\cdot y\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z\\cdot z}{5\\cdot y\\cdot 5\\cdot y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{z}{5y}\\cdot \\frac{z}{5y}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{z}{5y})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity and simplify using the rules of absolute value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{z}{5y})}^{2}} & =|\\frac{z}{5y}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{|5y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{|5|\\cdot |y|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|z|}{5|y|}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
